- rollout_summaries/2026-08-30T10-04-53-PTRd-media_auth_p1_p2_entry_flow_design.md (cwd=/Users/vsiyo/Desktop/创业项目/自媒体创作Agent, rollout_path=/Users/vsiyo/.codex/sessions/2026/08/30/rollout-2026-08-30T18-04-53-01a05221-116b-7952-a60f-e0e3b4686ae7.jsonl, updated_at=2026-08-30T10:30:43+00:00, thread_id=01a05221-116b-7952-a60f-e0e3b4686ae7, design only; no implementation or validation)

### keywords

- OpenClaw Media, P1, P2, authentication, `openclaw_session`, `GET /openclaw/auth/entry-state`, `WorkspaceResolver`, Feishu, `rememberMe: false`, multi-account

## User preferences

- when the user clarified: "进入P1这个然后点击右边变成P2，如果有保存的登陆状态，直接选择即可，对于左边也同理" -> model P1 as an explicit personal/organization chooser and P2 as the selected branch's symmetric authentication/session state [Task 1]
- when visual references support a proposed interaction and the user asks whether it was understood -> restate the interaction model and distinguish the design clarification from authoritative product/security instructions before editing [Task 1]

## Reusable knowledge

- The contract has one server-managed HttpOnly `openclaw_session`, `absoluteLifetimeSeconds: 28800`, and `rememberMe: false`. Phase-one "saved login state" therefore means only the current browser's valid server session; do not use `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, or `document.cookie` for persistent or multi-account state. [Task 1]
- P1 must remain visible and require an explicit card choice even when a cookie exists. P2 then checks the selected mode: personal requires `personal_web/internal`; organization requires `organization_lark/lark` with active membership, workspace, and Feishu binding. [Task 1]
- A matching session may show masked identity and a deliberate continue action. Missing, expired, revoked, or mismatched sessions fall back to password login or, only when needed, Feishu OAuth/QR, without account or tenant enumeration. [Task 1]
- Keep the strict `/openclaw/media/api/session` response unchanged. The proposed read-only phase-one surface is `GET /openclaw/auth/entry-state?mode=personal|organization`; any future activation/switch mutation must preserve same-origin checks, `X-OpenClaw-CSRF`, and appropriate session rotation. [Task 1]
- Relevant authority and checks: `openclaw-bot-center/contracts/media_web_business_pages.openapi.yaml`, `openclaw-bot-center/contracts/media-auth-route-contract.json`, `openclaw-tag-router/openclaw_app/adapters/http_api.py`, `openclaw-tag-router/openclaw_app/account/workspace_resolution.py`, `npm run qa:media-login-contract`, and `npm run build:media`. [Task 1]

## Failures and how to do differently

- This rollout is design clarification only. Do not claim code, tests, SSOT, commit, deployment, or feature completion until a later implementation provides that evidence. [Task 1]
- Symptom: "saved login" is interpreted as a multi-account picker. Cause: conflating current-session reuse with persistence. Fix: keep phase one to the opaque current server session; multi-account support requires a new contract covering storage, revocation, expiry, and security policy. [Task 1]
- Symptom: UX needs extra entry data. Fix: add a separate approved read-only surface rather than widening the strict `/openclaw/media/api/session` response. [Task 1]

